/-!
# Comparing the ph topology with the fppf topology (Stacks 0DBU)

An fppf covering of schemes is a ph covering (Stacks 0DBT,
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsPHCovering.of_mem_fppfPrecoverage`).  Consequently the underlying category
of a chosen big ph site carries a second, coarser topology — the one generated by its bounded
fppf covering families — and on the common slice category over an object `S` the identity
functor gives a comparison morphism `ε : (Sch/S)_ph ⟶ (Sch/S)_fppf`.  Its direct image is the
identity on underlying presheaves, and its inverse image sends an fppf sheaf to the ph
sheafification of its underlying presheaf.  Composing `ε` with the comparison of the fppf
topology to a coarser one compares the ph topology with the Zariski, étale, smooth and syntomic
topologies of Stacks 03FF.

## Main definitions

* `CategoryTheory.changeOfTopologyMorphism` — the change-of-topology morphism of topoi attached
  to a pair of topologies on one category, the source of the morphism carrying the finer one.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.phAssociatedBigFppfSite` — the same size-bounded category of schemes as a
  chosen big ph site, with its bounded fppf covering families; this is the "suitable choice of
  sites" the comparison needs, in the sense of Stacks 03FF.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.phToBigFppfMorphism` — the comparison `ε`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.phToZariskiMorphism`, `AlgebraicGeometry.phToEtaleMorphism`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.phToSmoothMorphism` and `AlgebraicGeometry.phToSyntomicMorphism` — the four
  comparisons obtained from `ε` by composition.

## Main results

* `CategoryTheory.Functor.preservesFiniteLimits_id_sheafPullback` — the functor on sheaves of
  sets induced by the identity functor from a topology to a finer one is left exact.  Together
  with `CategoryTheory.Functor.isContinuous_id_of_le` these are the two conditions of
  Stacks 00X1, so the identity functor is a morphism of sites whenever the topology it is read
  from is the coarser one: `CategoryTheory.changeOfTopology_isMorphismOfSites`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isPHCoveringInCutoff_of_isFppfCovering`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.fppfBounded_eq_phFppfBounded`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.phFppfCovering_isSite` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.phFppfCovering_has_representative` — the fppf coverings chosen by a big ph
  site form a site with enough representatives, which is what makes the associated big fppf
  site exist.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.bigFppfOverTopology_le_bigPHOverTopology` — the fppf topology of the common
  slice category is coarser than its ph topology, which is what makes the identity functor
  continuous.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.phToFppf_isContinuous` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.phToFppf_preservesFiniteLimits` — the two conditions of Stacks 00X1 for
  `ε`: the identity functor of the common slice, read from the fppf site to the ph site, is
  continuous and its induced functor on sheaves of sets is left exact.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.phToFppf_isMorphismOfSites` — **Stacks 0DBU**: `ε` is the morphism of
  sites given by the identity functor on underlying categories.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.phToBigFppf_pushforward_comp_sheafToPresheaf` — **Stacks 0DBU**: `ε_*` is
  the identity on underlying presheaves.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.phToBigFppf_inverseImageIso` — **Stacks 0DBU**: `ε⁻¹` is ph sheafification
  of the underlying presheaf of the fppf sheaf.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.phToCoarser_pushforward_comp_sheafToPresheaf` — the direct image of a
  composite comparison is again the identity on underlying presheaves.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.phToZariski_pushforward_comp_sheafToPresheaf`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.phToEtale_pushforward_comp_sheafToPresheaf`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.phToSmooth_pushforward_comp_sheafToPresheaf` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.phToSyntomic_pushforward_comp_sheafToPresheaf` — **Stacks 0DBU**: by
  composition the ph topology is compared with the Zariski, étale, smooth and syntomic
  topologies.

## Implementation notes

The associated fppf site has the same cutoff, covering bound and covering ordinal as the given
ph site, and no prescribed initial schemes or coverings, so the two sites have the same
underlying category and hence literally the same slices.  This is what "with suitable choices
of sites" asks for: one category of schemes carrying both topologies, so that the comparison is
induced by the identity functor and not by an equivalence.  Nothing here is tagged with
Stacks 03FF: the construction is the one already carried by
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.toBigZariskiSite` and its companions, applied to a different
category, and `AlgebraicGeometry.phAssociatedBigEtaleSite` — the étale analogue of
this site — carries no attribute either.

A morphism of sites `f : D ⟶ C` is, by Stacks 00X1, a continuous functor `u : C ⥤ D` in the
*opposite* direction whose associated functor `u_s` on sheaves of sets is exact.  For
`ε : (Sch/S)_ph ⟶ (Sch/S)_fppf` the functor `u` is therefore the identity of the slice, read
from the fppf site to the ph site, and the continuity it has to satisfy is that an fppf covering
sieve is a ph covering sieve.  It is this direction, and the fact that `u` is the identity, that
pin the comparison down as the one of Stacks 0DBU rather than some other morphism between the
two topoi: `AlgebraicGeometry.phToBigFppfMorphism` is `CategoryTheory.changeOfTopologyMorphism`
applied to `𝟭` of the common slice, so its direct image is restriction along the identity and
its inverse image the induced functor on sheaves of sets, by construction.  This is why the
first identification below holds by `rfl` rather than up to a chosen isomorphism, and why the
second one is the canonical comparison and not merely some isomorphism of the right type.

The comparison `ε` itself is a construction and carries no attribute: constructing an object
the tag asserts properties of is not proving those properties.  The remark's first sentence is
registered instead on `AlgebraicGeometry.phToFppf_isMorphismOfSites`: the assertion that
sentence makes about the construction is that the identity functor of the one underlying
category is a morphism of sites, and it is from that morphism of sites that `ε` is read off.
The remark's middle sentence is registered on the two identifications of `ε_*` and `ε⁻¹`, and
its last one on the four theorems about the composite comparisons.  Each of those four names
the composition and states of it the same property that makes `ε` a comparison of the ph with
the fppf topology — the direct image is the identity on underlying presheaves — so it says that
the composite compares the ph topology with the coarser one, and not just that some morphism
between the two topoi exists.  The machinery the four rest on belongs to other tags: the
composition of morphisms of topoi to Stacks 03CC, and the fact that a chosen covering family
for a coarser topology is a chosen fppf covering family to Stacks 03FF.

The two conditions of Stacks 00X1 are bundled by `IsMorphismOfSites`, whose category and sheaf
universes are independent, and not by `CategoryTheory.Functor.IsMorphismOfSites`, which is
stated for a `CategoryTheory.SmallCategory` and so does not apply: the slice of a big site has
its objects in `Type (u + 1)` and its morphisms in `Type u`, the universes of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme`.  They are also recorded one at a time, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.phToFppf_isContinuous` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.phToFppf_preservesFiniteLimits`, because it is in that form that the
construction of `ε` and of the composite comparisons uses them.  The composition of Stacks 03CC
is taken on the morphisms of topoi, by `CategoryTheory.MorphismOfTopoi.comp`, rather than on the
morphisms of sites.

That `u_s` is exact is automatic for the identity functor: it is a left adjoint, so right
exactness is free, and the left Kan extension along the identity is the identity, so `u_s` is
the forgetful functor to presheaves followed by sheafification, both of which are left exact.
The identification of `ε⁻¹` with ph sheafification is read off the same computation.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 00X1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00X1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00XC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00XC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03CC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03CC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03FF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03FF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DBT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DBT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DBU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DBU)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Cardinal

universe u

namespace CategoryTheory

/-- Localizing a topology at an object is monotone in the topology: a sieve of a slice object
covers for the localization exactly when its image covers in the ambient topology. -/
theorem GrothendieckTopology.over_le_over_of_le {C : Type*} [Category C]
    {J K : GrothendieckTopology C} (h : J ≤ K) (X : C) :
    J.over X ≤ K.over X := by
  intro Y S hS
  rw [GrothendieckTopology.mem_over_iff] at hS ⊢
  exact h _ hS

section ChangeOfTopology

variable (C : Type (u + 1)) [Category.{u} C]

/-- Left Kan extension along the opposite of the identity functor is the identity: both are left
adjoint to restriction along the identity. -/
def Functor.opLanIdIso :
    ((𝟭 C).op.lan : (Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type (u + 1)) ⥤ (Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type (u + 1))) ≅
      𝟭 (Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type (u + 1)) := by
  simpa only [Functor.whiskeringLeft_obj_id] using
    Adjunction.leftAdjointUniq ((𝟭 C).op.lanAdjunction (Type (u + 1))) Adjunction.id

/-- **The exactness condition of Stacks 00X1 for a change of topology.** The functor `u_s` on
sheaves of sets induced by the identity functor, read from a topology `J` to a finer topology
`K` on the same category, is left exact: the left Kan extension along the identity is the
identity, so `u_s` is the forgetful functor to presheaves followed by `K`-sheafification.

Right exactness is automatic, `u_s` being a left adjoint
(`CategoryTheory.Functor.preservesFiniteColimits_sheafPullback`), and continuity of the identity
functor is `CategoryTheory.Functor.isContinuous_id_of_le`.  So together these say that the
identity functor is a morphism of sites `(C, K) ⟶ (C, J)`. -/
@[sga "4 III 1.3" "clause 5), special case", sga "4 III 2.5" "special case"]
theorem Functor.preservesFiniteLimits_id_sheafPullback (J K : GrothendieckTopology C)
    [(𝟭 C).IsContinuous J K] :
    PreservesFiniteLimits ((𝟭 C).sheafPullback (Type (u + 1)) J K) := by
  have : PreservesFiniteLimits
      ((𝟭 C).op.lan : (Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type (u + 1)) ⥤ (Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type (u + 1))) :=
    preservesFiniteLimits_of_natIso (Functor.opLanIdIso C).symm
  exact Functor.sheafPullbackConstruction.preservesFiniteLimits (𝟭 C) (Type (u + 1)) J K

/-- **The identity functor of a change of topology is a morphism of sites.** Given two
topologies `J ≤ K` on one category, the identity functor read from `(C, J)` to `(C, K)` is
continuous (`CategoryTheory.Functor.isContinuous_id_of_le`) and the functor it induces on
sheaves of sets is left exact (`CategoryTheory.Functor.preservesFiniteLimits_id_sheafPullback`),
which are the two conditions of Stacks 00X1.  So the identity functor is a morphism of sites
`(C, K) ⟶ (C, J)`, and `CategoryTheory.changeOfTopologyMorphism` below is the morphism of topoi
Stacks 00XC attaches to it.

This is stated for the universe-polymorphic `IsMorphismOfSites`, the morphism-of-sites condition
on sheaves of sets valued in `Type (u + 1)`.  `CategoryTheory.Functor.IsMorphismOfSites` is the
same condition on a `CategoryTheory.SmallCategory`, where objects and morphisms share a
universe; it does not apply to a category like the slice of a big site, whose objects live one
universe above its morphisms. -/
theorem changeOfTopology_isMorphismOfSites (J K : GrothendieckTopology C) (h : J ≤ K) :
    IsMorphismOfSites.{u + 1} (𝟭 C) J K :=
  have := Functor.isContinuous_id_of_le J K h
  { __ := ‹(𝟭 C).IsContinuous J K›
    hasExactLeftAdjoint :=
      ⟨(𝟭 C).sheafPullback (Type (u + 1)) J K,
        ⟨(𝟭 C).sheafAdjunctionContinuous (Type (u + 1)) J K⟩,
        Functor.preservesFiniteLimits_id_sheafPullback C J K⟩ }

/-- **The change-of-topology morphism of topoi.** Given two topologies `J ≤ K` on one category,
the identity functor is continuous from `(C, K)` to `(C, J)` and its induced functor on sheaves
of sets is exact, so Stacks 00XC attaches to it a morphism of topoi
`Sh(C, K) ⟶ Sh(C, J)` whose direct image is restriction along the identity functor and whose
inverse image is the induced functor on sheaves of sets. -/
def changeOfTopologyMorphism (J K : GrothendieckTopology C) [(𝟭 C).IsContinuous J K] :
    MorphismOfTopoi (Sheaf K (Type (u + 1))) (Sheaf J (Type (u + 1))) where
  pushforward := (𝟭 C).sheafPushforwardContinuous (Type (u + 1)) J K
  inverseImage := (𝟭 C).sheafPullback (Type (u + 1)) J K
  adj := (𝟭 C).sheafAdjunctionContinuous (Type (u + 1)) J K
  preservesFiniteLimits := Functor.preservesFiniteLimits_id_sheafPullback C J K

/-- **The direct image of a change-of-topology morphism is the identity on underlying
presheaves**: it is restriction along the identity functor. -/
theorem changeOfTopologyMorphism_pushforward_comp_sheafToPresheaf
    (J K : GrothendieckTopology C) [(𝟭 C).IsContinuous J K] :
    (changeOfTopologyMorphism C J K).pushforward ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type (u + 1)) =
      sheafToPresheaf K (Type (u + 1)) :=
  rfl

/-- **The inverse image of a change-of-topology morphism is sheafification for the finer
topology** of the underlying presheaf.  The isomorphism is the canonical one: it is the
comparison of the induced functor with its construction as a left Kan extension followed by
sheafification, composed with the identification of the left Kan extension along the identity
functor with the identity. -/
def changeOfTopologyMorphism_inverseImageIso (J K : GrothendieckTopology C)
    [(𝟭 C).IsContinuous J K] :
    (changeOfTopologyMorphism C J K).inverseImage ≅
      sheafToPresheaf J (Type (u + 1)) ⋙ presheafToSheaf K (Type (u + 1)) := by
  refine Functor.sheafPullbackConstruction.sheafPullbackIso (𝟭 C) (Type (u + 1)) J K ≪≫ ?_
  change sheafToPresheaf J (Type (u + 1)) ⋙
      (𝟭 C).op.lan ⋙ presheafToSheaf K (Type (u + 1)) ≅
    sheafToPresheaf J (Type (u + 1)) ⋙ presheafToSheaf K (Type (u + 1))
  exact Functor.isoWhiskerLeft (sheafToPresheaf J (Type (u + 1)))
    (Functor.isoWhiskerRight (Functor.opLanIdIso C) (presheafToSheaf K (Type (u + 1))))

end ChangeOfTopology

end CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-! ### The fppf covering families of the category of a chosen big ph site -/

/-- Being an fppf covering family of a size-bounded category of schemes is membership of the
image presieve in the fppf precoverage of all schemes. -/
public theorem isFppfCovering_iff_presieve₀_map {κ : Cardinal.{u}}
    (E : Covering.{u + 1, u, u + 1} (SchemeBelow κ)) :
    IsFppfCovering E ↔ (E.2.map (schemeBelowInclusion κ)).presieve₀ ∈
      Scheme.fppfPrecoverage ((schemeBelowInclusion κ).obj E.1) := by
  rw [PreZeroHypercover.presieve₀_map]
  exact Iff.rfl

/-- An fppf covering family of a size-bounded category of schemes is a ph covering family there,
both conditions being read off the image of the family in all schemes.

This is Stacks 0DBT, `AlgebraicGeometry.IsPHCovering.of_mem_fppfPrecoverage`, transported to a
cutoff category.  No attribute is attached: 0DBT already carries a bare attribute there, so it
is covered in full and a suffixed attribute naming a clause of it would be redundant. -/
public theorem isPHCoveringInCutoff_of_isFppfCovering {κ : Cardinal.{u}}
    (E : Covering.{u + 1, u, u + 1} (SchemeBelow κ)) (hE : IsFppfCovering E) :
    IsPHCoveringInCutoff E :=
  IsPHCovering.of_mem_fppfPrecoverage _ _ ((isFppfCovering_iff_presieve₀_map E).mp hE)

/-- A chosen covering family of a big ph site which is in addition fppf is the same thing as a
bounded fppf covering family, because an fppf covering is a ph covering. -/
public theorem fppfBounded_eq_phFppfBounded (B : BigPHSite.{u}) (E : Covering B.Schemes) :
    (B.IsCovering E ∧ IsFppfCovering E) ↔
      CovBounded (IsFppfCovering (κ := B.cutoff)) B.coveringBound E := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨⟨_, hbound⟩, hfppf⟩
    exact ⟨hfppf, hbound⟩
  · rintro ⟨hfppf, hbound⟩
    exact ⟨⟨isPHCoveringInCutoff_of_isFppfCovering E hfppf, hbound⟩, hfppf⟩

/-- The fppf subcollection of the chosen coverings of a big ph site satisfies the site
axioms. -/
public theorem phFppfCovering_isSite (B : BigPHSite.{u}) :
    IsSite (fun E : Covering B.Schemes ↦ B.IsCovering E ∧ IsFppfCovering E) := by
  have heq : (fun E : Covering B.Schemes ↦ B.IsCovering E ∧ IsFppfCovering E) =
      (fun E : Covering B.Schemes ↦ B.IsCovering E ∧
        (E.2.map B.inclusion).presieve₀ ∈ Scheme.fppfPrecoverage (B.inclusion.obj E.1)) :=
    funext fun E ↦ propext (and_congr_right' (isFppfCovering_iff_presieve₀_map E))
  rw [heq]
  exact isSite_and_precoverage B.inclusion B.IsCovering Scheme.fppfPrecoverage B.isSite

/-- Every fppf covering of the underlying category of a big ph site is combinatorially
equivalent to one of the site's chosen coverings, which is then again fppf. -/
public theorem phFppfCovering_has_representative (B : BigPHSite.{u}) (E : Covering B.Schemes)
    (hE : IsFppfCovering E) :
    ∃ E' : Covering B.Schemes,
      (B.IsCovering E' ∧ IsFppfCovering E') ∧ Covering.CombEquiv E E' := by
  obtain ⟨E', hB, hCE⟩ := B.covering_representative E (isPHCoveringInCutoff_of_isFppfCovering E hE)
  exact ⟨E', ⟨hB, (isFppfCovering_iff_presieve₀_map E').mpr
    ((map_mem_iff_of_combEquiv B.inclusion Scheme.fppfPrecoverage hCE).mp
      ((isFppfCovering_iff_presieve₀_map E).mp hE))⟩, hCE⟩

/-! ### The fppf site on the category of a chosen big ph site -/

/-- **The fppf site on the underlying category of a chosen big ph site.** Its cutoff, covering
bound and covering ordinal are the ph site's own, and it prescribes no initial schemes or
coverings, so its underlying category is literally that of the ph site and the two topologies
live on one category.  This is the "suitable choice of sites" of Stacks 03FF which the
comparison of Stacks 0DBU needs. -/
public abbrev phAssociatedBigFppfSite (B : BigPHSite.{u}) : BigFppfSite.{u} := by
  letI : Small.{u} (∅ : Set Scheme.{u}) := inferInstance
  letI : Small.{u + 1} (∅ : Set (Covering B.Schemes)) := inferInstance
  have hpred : (fun E : Covering B.Schemes ↦ B.IsCovering E ∧ IsFppfCovering E) =
      CovBounded (IsFppfCovering (κ := B.cutoff)) B.coveringBound :=
    funext fun E ↦ propext (fppfBounded_eq_phFppfBounded B E)
  have hsite : IsSite (CovBounded (IsFppfCovering (κ := B.cutoff)) B.coveringBound) := by
    rw [← hpred]
    exact phFppfCovering_isSite B
  exact
    { initialSchemes := ∅
      initialSchemes_small := inferInstance
      cutoff := B.cutoff
      aleph0_lt_cutoff := B.aleph0_lt_cutoff
      cutoff_isStrongPrelimit := B.cutoff_isStrongPrelimit
      aleph0_lt_cutoff_cof := B.aleph0_lt_cutoff_cof
      initialSchemes_mem := by simp
      initialCoverings := ∅
      initialCoverings_small := inferInstance
      initialCoverings_supported := by simp
      coveringBound := B.coveringBound
      coveringOrdinal := B.coveringOrdinal
      coveringOrdinal_isSuccLimit := B.coveringOrdinal_isSuccLimit
      initialCoverings_mem := by simp
      coverings_isSite := hsite
      fppf_has_representative := fun E hE ↦ by
        obtain ⟨E', hE', hEq⟩ := phFppfCovering_has_representative B E hE
        exact ⟨E', (fppfBounded_eq_phFppfBounded B E').mp hE', hEq⟩ }

/-- The associated fppf site has the ph site's own size cutoff, so the two sites have the same
underlying category. -/
public theorem phAssociatedBigFppfSite_cutoff (B : BigPHSite.{u}) :
    (phAssociatedBigFppfSite B).cutoff = B.cutoff := rfl

/-- The chosen covering families of the associated fppf site are the chosen ph covering families
which are fppf. -/
public theorem phAssociatedBigFppfSite_isCovering_iff (B : BigPHSite.{u})
    (E : Covering B.Schemes) :
    (phAssociatedBigFppfSite B).IsCovering E ↔ (B.IsCovering E ∧ IsFppfCovering E) :=
  (fppfBounded_eq_phFppfBounded B E).symm

/-- Every covering for the associated fppf topology is a covering for the ph topology. -/
public theorem phAssociatedFppfTopology_le_phTopology (B : BigPHSite.{u}) :
    (phAssociatedBigFppfSite B).topology ≤ B.topology :=
  Precoverage.toGrothendieck_mono fun _ _ ⟨E, hR, hE⟩ ↦
    ⟨E, hR, ((phAssociatedBigFppfSite_isCovering_iff B _).mp hE).1⟩

/-- **The comparison of topologies on the common slice category.** Every fppf covering sieve of
an object of the slice over `X` is a ph covering sieve there; this is what makes the identity
functor continuous. -/
public theorem bigFppfOverTopology_le_bigPHOverTopology (B : BigPHSite.{u}) (X : B.Schemes) :
    BigFppfOver.topology (phAssociatedBigFppfSite B) X.1 X.2 ≤ B.topology.over X :=
  GrothendieckTopology.over_le_over_of_le (phAssociatedFppfTopology_le_phTopology B) X

/-! ### The comparison `ε` -/

/-- **The continuity condition of Stacks 00X1 for `ε`**: the identity functor of the common
slice category, read from the fppf site to the ph site as Stacks 00X1 requires of the functor
underlying `ε : (Sch/S)_ph ⟶ (Sch/S)_fppf`, is continuous — restriction along it takes ph
sheaves to fppf sheaves. -/
public theorem phToFppf_isContinuous (B : BigPHSite.{u}) (X : B.Schemes) :
    (𝟭 (Over X)).IsContinuous
      (BigFppfOver.topology (phAssociatedBigFppfSite B) X.1 X.2)
      (B.topology.over X) :=
  Functor.isContinuous_id_of_le _ _ (bigFppfOverTopology_le_bigPHOverTopology B X)

/-- **The comparison `ε : (Sch/S)_ph ⟶ (Sch/S)_fppf` of Stacks 0DBU**: the morphism of topoi
which Stacks 00XC attaches to the identity functor of the common slice category, read from the
fppf site to the ph site.  It is therefore the comparison of Stacks 0DBU and not some other
morphism between the two topoi: its direct image is restriction along the identity functor and
its inverse image the induced functor on sheaves of sets, both by construction.

No attribute is attached: this constructs the comparison, and the properties of it that
Stacks 0DBU asserts are the two identifications below, which carry the attributes. -/
public def phToBigFppfMorphism (B : BigPHSite.{u}) (X : B.Schemes) :
    MorphismOfTopoi
      (Sheaf (B.topology.over X) (Type (u + 1)))
      (Sheaf (BigFppfOver.topology (phAssociatedBigFppfSite B) X.1 X.2) (Type (u + 1))) :=
  haveI := phToFppf_isContinuous B X
  changeOfTopologyMorphism (Over X)
    (BigFppfOver.topology (phAssociatedBigFppfSite B) X.1 X.2) (B.topology.over X)

/-- **The exactness condition of Stacks 00X1 for `ε`**: the inverse image of `ε` is left exact.
Since the inverse image is the functor on sheaves of sets induced by the identity functor of the
common slice (`AlgebraicGeometry.phToBigFppf_inverseImageIso`), this together with
`AlgebraicGeometry.phToFppf_isContinuous` is exactly what Stacks 00X1 asks of a morphism of
sites. -/
public theorem phToFppf_preservesFiniteLimits (B : BigPHSite.{u}) (X : B.Schemes) :
    PreservesFiniteLimits (phToBigFppfMorphism B X).inverseImage :=
  (phToBigFppfMorphism B X).preservesFiniteLimits

/-- **Stacks 0DBU: `ε` is the morphism of sites given by the identity functor on underlying
categories.** The two sites have the one underlying category, the slice over `X` of the common
category of schemes, and the identity functor of it, read from the fppf site to the ph site,
satisfies the two conditions of Stacks 00X1: it is continuous and the functor it induces on
sheaves of sets is left exact.  So it is a morphism of sites `(Sch/S)_ph ⟶ (Sch/S)_fppf`, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.phToBigFppfMorphism` is the morphism of topoi Stacks 00XC attaches to it. -/
@[stacks 0DBU "the comparison is the morphism of sites given by the identity functor on
  underlying categories"]
public theorem phToFppf_isMorphismOfSites (B : BigPHSite.{u}) (X : B.Schemes) :
    IsMorphismOfSites.{u + 1} (𝟭 (Over X))
      (BigFppfOver.topology (phAssociatedBigFppfSite B) X.1 X.2) (B.topology.over X) :=
  changeOfTopology_isMorphismOfSites (Over X)
    (BigFppfOver.topology (phAssociatedBigFppfSite B) X.1 X.2) (B.topology.over X)
    (bigFppfOverTopology_le_bigPHOverTopology B X)

/-- **Stacks 0DBU: `ε_*` is the identity on underlying presheaves.** Forming the direct image of
a ph sheaf and then forgetting the fppf sheaf condition gives back the presheaf one started
from, because the direct image is restriction along the identity functor of the common slice
category.  The two sides are equal, not merely isomorphic. -/
@[stacks 0DBU "the direct image is the identity on underlying presheaves"]
public theorem phToBigFppf_pushforward_comp_sheafToPresheaf (B : BigPHSite.{u})
    (X : B.Schemes) :
    (phToBigFppfMorphism B X).pushforward ⋙
        sheafToPresheaf (BigFppfOver.topology (phAssociatedBigFppfSite B) X.1 X.2)
          (Type (u + 1)) =
      sheafToPresheaf (B.topology.over X) (Type (u + 1)) :=
  have := phToFppf_isContinuous B X
  changeOfTopologyMorphism_pushforward_comp_sheafToPresheaf (Over X)
    (BigFppfOver.topology (phAssociatedBigFppfSite B) X.1 X.2) (B.topology.over X)

/-- **Stacks 0DBU: `ε⁻¹` associates to an fppf sheaf its ph sheafification.** The inverse image
is the functor on sheaves of sets induced by the identity functor of the common slice, and the
left Kan extension along the identity is the identity, so the inverse image is the forgetful
functor to presheaves followed by ph sheafification.

The isomorphism is the canonical one, not just some isomorphism of the right type: `ε` is by
construction the change-of-topology morphism of the identity functor, and the comparison is
`CategoryTheory.changeOfTopologyMorphism_inverseImageIso`, built from the construction of the
induced functor as a left Kan extension followed by sheafification. -/
@[stacks 0DBU "the inverse image is the ph sheafification of an fppf sheaf"]
public def phToBigFppf_inverseImageIso (B : BigPHSite.{u}) (X : B.Schemes) :
    (phToBigFppfMorphism B X).inverseImage ≅
      sheafToPresheaf (BigFppfOver.topology (phAssociatedBigFppfSite B) X.1 X.2)
          (Type (u + 1)) ⋙
        presheafToSheaf (B.topology.over X) (Type (u + 1)) :=
  haveI := phToFppf_isContinuous B X
  changeOfTopologyMorphism_inverseImageIso (Over X)
    (BigFppfOver.topology (phAssociatedBigFppfSite B) X.1 X.2) (B.topology.over X)

/-! ### The comparisons with the coarser topologies, by composition

Stacks 0DBU closes by observing that composing `ε` compares the ph topology with the syntomic,
smooth, étale and Zariski topologies.  The four definitions below form those compositions, and
the four theorems beside them identify each composite as a comparison of the ph topology with
the coarser one in the same sense as `ε` itself: its direct image is the identity on underlying
presheaves.  It is those four theorems that carry the attribute for the remark's last
sentence. -/

/-- A topology generated by a sub-collection of a big fppf site's chosen covering families is
coarser than the topology the site generates. -/
public theorem chosenTopology_le_topology (B : BigFppfSite.{u})
    (P : Covering B.Schemes → Prop) (hP : ∀ E, P E → B.IsCovering E) :
    (B.chosenPrecoverage P).toGrothendieck ≤ B.topology :=
  Precoverage.toGrothendieck_mono fun _ _ ⟨E, hR, hE⟩ ↦ ⟨E, hR, hP _ hE⟩

/-- The same, localized at an object: a coarser chosen topology of Stacks 03FF on the slice over
`X` is coarser than the fppf topology there. -/
public theorem chosenOverTopology_le_bigFppfOverTopology (B : BigFppfSite.{u})
    (P : Covering B.Schemes → Prop) (hP : ∀ E, P E → B.IsCovering E) (X : B.Schemes) :
    (B.chosenPrecoverage P).toGrothendieck.over X ≤ B.topology.over X :=
  GrothendieckTopology.over_le_over_of_le (chosenTopology_le_topology B P hP) X

/-- **The comparison of the ph topology with a coarser topology, by composition.** Given a
topology on the common slice category coarser than the associated fppf topology, composing the
corresponding change-of-topology morphism with `ε` compares the ph topology with it.  This is
the composition of Stacks 03CC, taken on morphisms of topoi. -/
public def phToCoarserMorphism (B : BigPHSite.{u}) (X : B.Schemes)
    (J : GrothendieckTopology (Over X))
    (hJ : J ≤ BigFppfOver.topology (phAssociatedBigFppfSite B) X.1 X.2) :
    MorphismOfTopoi (Sheaf (B.topology.over X) (Type (u + 1))) (Sheaf J (Type (u + 1))) :=
  haveI := Functor.isContinuous_id_of_le J _ hJ
  (changeOfTopologyMorphism (Over X) J
      (BigFppfOver.topology (phAssociatedBigFppfSite B) X.1 X.2)).comp
    (phToBigFppfMorphism B X)

/-- **A composite comparison is again the identity on underlying presheaves.** The direct image
of `AlgebraicGeometry.phToCoarserMorphism` is the direct image of `ε` followed by that of the
change-of-topology morphism from the fppf topology to the coarser one, and each of the two is
restriction along the identity functor of the common slice category; so the composite direct
image is too.  Together with the typing — a morphism of topoi from ph sheaves to `J`-sheaves —
this says that the composite is a comparison of the ph topology with `J` in the same sense as
`ε` is a comparison of the ph topology with the fppf topology, and not merely some morphism
between the two topoi.  The two sides are equal, not merely isomorphic. -/
public theorem phToCoarser_pushforward_comp_sheafToPresheaf (B : BigPHSite.{u}) (X : B.Schemes)
    (J : GrothendieckTopology (Over X))
    (hJ : J ≤ BigFppfOver.topology (phAssociatedBigFppfSite B) X.1 X.2) :
    (phToCoarserMorphism B X J hJ).pushforward ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type (u + 1)) =
      sheafToPresheaf (B.topology.over X) (Type (u + 1)) :=
  rfl

/-- **The comparison of the ph topology with the Zariski topology of Stacks 03FF**, obtained by
composing `ε` with the change-of-topology morphism from the fppf to the Zariski topology.

The attribute for this clause of Stacks 0DBU is carried by
`AlgebraicGeometry.phToZariski_pushforward_comp_sheafToPresheaf`, which identifies this
composite as a comparison of the two topologies and not merely as a morphism of topoi. -/
public def phToZariskiMorphism (B : BigPHSite.{u}) (X : B.Schemes) :
    MorphismOfTopoi (Sheaf (B.topology.over X) (Type (u + 1)))
      (Sheaf ((phAssociatedBigFppfSite B).zariskiTopology.over X) (Type (u + 1))) :=
  phToCoarserMorphism B X _
    (chosenOverTopology_le_bigFppfOverTopology (phAssociatedBigFppfSite B)
      (phAssociatedBigFppfSite B).zariskiCovering (fun _ hE ↦ hE.1) X)

/-- **Stacks 0DBU: by composition the ph topology is compared with the Zariski topology.**
`AlgebraicGeometry.phToZariskiMorphism`, the composition of `ε` with the change-of-topology
morphism from the fppf to the Zariski topology, is a comparison of the ph topology with the
Zariski topology of Stacks 03FF: it is a morphism of topoi from ph sheaves to Zariski sheaves
whose direct image is the identity on underlying presheaves, as `ε`'s own is. -/
@[stacks 0DBU "by composition, the comparison of the ph topology with the Zariski topology"]
public theorem phToZariski_pushforward_comp_sheafToPresheaf (B : BigPHSite.{u})
    (X : B.Schemes) :
    (phToZariskiMorphism B X).pushforward ⋙
        sheafToPresheaf ((phAssociatedBigFppfSite B).zariskiTopology.over X) (Type (u + 1)) =
      sheafToPresheaf (B.topology.over X) (Type (u + 1)) :=
  phToCoarser_pushforward_comp_sheafToPresheaf B X _ _

/-- **The comparison of the ph topology with the étale topology of Stacks 03FF**, obtained by
composing `ε` with the change-of-topology morphism from the fppf to the étale topology.

The attribute for this clause of Stacks 0DBU is carried by
`AlgebraicGeometry.phToEtale_pushforward_comp_sheafToPresheaf`, which identifies this composite
as a comparison of the two topologies and not merely as a morphism of topoi. -/
public def phToEtaleMorphism (B : BigPHSite.{u}) (X : B.Schemes) :
    MorphismOfTopoi (Sheaf (B.topology.over X) (Type (u + 1)))
      (Sheaf ((phAssociatedBigFppfSite B).etaleTopology.over X) (Type (u + 1))) :=
  phToCoarserMorphism B X _
    (chosenOverTopology_le_bigFppfOverTopology (phAssociatedBigFppfSite B)
      (phAssociatedBigFppfSite B).etaleCovering (fun _ hE ↦ hE.1) X)

/-- **Stacks 0DBU: by composition the ph topology is compared with the étale topology.**
`AlgebraicGeometry.phToEtaleMorphism`, the composition of `ε` with the change-of-topology
morphism from the fppf to the étale topology, is a comparison of the ph topology with the étale
topology of Stacks 03FF: it is a morphism of topoi from ph sheaves to étale sheaves whose
direct image is the identity on underlying presheaves, as `ε`'s own is. -/
@[stacks 0DBU "by composition, the comparison of the ph topology with the étale topology"]
public theorem phToEtale_pushforward_comp_sheafToPresheaf (B : BigPHSite.{u}) (X : B.Schemes) :
    (phToEtaleMorphism B X).pushforward ⋙
        sheafToPresheaf ((phAssociatedBigFppfSite B).etaleTopology.over X) (Type (u + 1)) =
      sheafToPresheaf (B.topology.over X) (Type (u + 1)) :=
  phToCoarser_pushforward_comp_sheafToPresheaf B X _ _

/-- **The comparison of the ph topology with the smooth topology of Stacks 03FF**, obtained by
composing `ε` with the change-of-topology morphism from the fppf to the smooth topology.

The attribute for this clause of Stacks 0DBU is carried by
`AlgebraicGeometry.phToSmooth_pushforward_comp_sheafToPresheaf`, which identifies this composite
as a comparison of the two topologies and not merely as a morphism of topoi. -/
public def phToSmoothMorphism (B : BigPHSite.{u}) (X : B.Schemes) :
    MorphismOfTopoi (Sheaf (B.topology.over X) (Type (u + 1)))
      (Sheaf ((phAssociatedBigFppfSite B).smoothTopology.over X) (Type (u + 1))) :=
  phToCoarserMorphism B X _
    (chosenOverTopology_le_bigFppfOverTopology (phAssociatedBigFppfSite B)
      (phAssociatedBigFppfSite B).smoothCovering (fun _ hE ↦ hE.1) X)

/-- **Stacks 0DBU: by composition the ph topology is compared with the smooth topology.**
`AlgebraicGeometry.phToSmoothMorphism`, the composition of `ε` with the change-of-topology
morphism from the fppf to the smooth topology, is a comparison of the ph topology with the
smooth topology of Stacks 03FF: it is a morphism of topoi from ph sheaves to smooth sheaves
whose direct image is the identity on underlying presheaves, as `ε`'s own is. -/
@[stacks 0DBU "by composition, the comparison of the ph topology with the smooth topology"]
public theorem phToSmooth_pushforward_comp_sheafToPresheaf (B : BigPHSite.{u}) (X : B.Schemes) :
    (phToSmoothMorphism B X).pushforward ⋙
        sheafToPresheaf ((phAssociatedBigFppfSite B).smoothTopology.over X) (Type (u + 1)) =
      sheafToPresheaf (B.topology.over X) (Type (u + 1)) :=
  phToCoarser_pushforward_comp_sheafToPresheaf B X _ _

/-- **The comparison of the ph topology with the syntomic topology of Stacks 03FF**, obtained by
composing `ε` with the change-of-topology morphism from the fppf to the syntomic topology.

The attribute for this clause of Stacks 0DBU is carried by
`AlgebraicGeometry.phToSyntomic_pushforward_comp_sheafToPresheaf`, which identifies this
composite as a comparison of the two topologies and not merely as a morphism of topoi. -/
public def phToSyntomicMorphism (B : BigPHSite.{u}) (X : B.Schemes) :
    MorphismOfTopoi (Sheaf (B.topology.over X) (Type (u + 1)))
      (Sheaf ((phAssociatedBigFppfSite B).syntomicTopology.over X) (Type (u + 1))) :=
  phToCoarserMorphism B X _
    (chosenOverTopology_le_bigFppfOverTopology (phAssociatedBigFppfSite B)
      (phAssociatedBigFppfSite B).syntomicCovering (fun _ hE ↦ hE.1) X)

/-- **Stacks 0DBU: by composition the ph topology is compared with the syntomic topology.**
`AlgebraicGeometry.phToSyntomicMorphism`, the composition of `ε` with the change-of-topology
morphism from the fppf to the syntomic topology, is a comparison of the ph topology with the
syntomic topology of Stacks 03FF: it is a morphism of topoi from ph sheaves to syntomic sheaves
whose direct image is the identity on underlying presheaves, as `ε`'s own is. -/
@[stacks 0DBU "by composition, the comparison of the ph topology with the syntomic topology"]
public theorem phToSyntomic_pushforward_comp_sheafToPresheaf (B : BigPHSite.{u})
    (X : B.Schemes) :
    (phToSyntomicMorphism B X).pushforward ⋙
        sheafToPresheaf ((phAssociatedBigFppfSite B).syntomicTopology.over X) (Type (u + 1)) =
      sheafToPresheaf (B.topology.over X) (Type (u + 1)) :=
  phToCoarser_pushforward_comp_sheafToPresheaf B X _ _

end AlgebraicGeometry

